---
layout: none
---
{%- comment -%}
  Lookup index for the masthead autocomplete (assets/js/arc42-autocomplete.js).

  This is deliberately NOT search.json. search.json carries the full body text
  and feeds lunr on /search/; this file carries titles and keywords only, so the
  dropdown can be scored with a plain prefix/substring ranker that stays
  predictable while the visitor types. Keeping them apart also keeps this file
  small enough to fetch on the first keystroke.

  Shape (array):  { "title", "type", "url", "tags" }
  type is "page" for site.pages, or the resource's own type
  ("book" | "article" | "talk" | "video") for /publikationen/ entries.

  Page exclusions mirror search.json's: the two form-result stubs and the 404
  page. On top of that, the six `layout: redirect` stubs (/books/, /articles/,
  /videos/, /talks/, /more/, /recommendations/ — see CLAUDE.md) are dropped:
  they render no content, they only bounce to /publikationen/, and offering the
  visitor a suggestion that immediately redirects elsewhere is a dead row.

  /info-msa-EN/ is dropped too, because it carries the SAME title as its German
  twin /info-msa/ ("Mastering Software Architectures"). Below 1024px the panel
  hides the URL column, so the two rows render pixel-identical — a choice
  between two things that look like the same thing. The German page is the
  canonical entry on a German site; the English one stays reachable through the
  lunr-backed /search/ page, which shows an excerpt and can tell them apart.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign lookup_pages = site.pages
      | where_exp: "p", "p.title"
      | where_exp: "p", "p.layout != 'redirect'"
      | where_exp: "p", "p.title != 'Super!'"
      | where_exp: "p", "p.title != 'OOPS!'"
      | where_exp: "p", "p.title != 'Sorry, Page Not Found (404)'"
      | where_exp: "p", "p.url != '/info-msa-EN/'" -%}
[
{% for page in lookup_pages -%}
  {"title": {{ page.title | jsonify }}, "type": "page", "url": {{ page.url | prepend: site.baseurl | jsonify }}, "tags": ""}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{% endfor -%}
{%- comment -%}
  site.pages does NOT include collection documents, so the ~50 /publikationen/
  entries need their own loop.

  The url points at the detail page when there is one, otherwise at the filtered
  listing plus the card's anchor. The anchor is the filename slug, derived the
  same way _includes/resource-item.html and search.json derive it — NOT
  `resource.id`, which Jekyll's DocumentDrop overrides with the document's
  internal id.

  `search` (the entry's extra keywords: authors, publisher, alternative
  spellings) becomes `tags`, which the scorer weighs below title matches.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if site.resources.size > 0 -%}
{%- if lookup_pages.size > 0 -%},{%- endif %}
{% for resource in site.resources -%}
  {%- assign r_anchor = resource.path | split: '/' | last | split: '.' | first -%}
  {%- if resource.detail -%}
    {%- assign r_url = resource.url | prepend: site.baseurl -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- capture r_url %}{{ site.baseurl }}/publikationen/?type={{ resource.type }}#{{ r_anchor }}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {"title": {{ resource.title | jsonify }}, "type": {{ resource.type | jsonify }}, "url": {{ r_url | jsonify }}, "tags": {{ resource.search | default: "" | jsonify }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
]
